74-no-glidept: the Glide pass-through device is not built (ADR-020)

qemu-3dfx's overlay wires two pass-through devices into the PC machine:
hw/3dfx (Glide, dispatching to a host libglide2x) and hw/mesa (OpenGL).
2ksbox retired the Glide pass-through in favour of the emulated Voodoo 2
(ADR-020, doc 21): no host wrapper is built or shipped, so the device
would only ever refuse. This takes hw/3dfx out of the build and the
machine while hw/mesa stays. The overlay directory is still copied in,
because qemu-3dfx's sign_commit stamps files in it; nothing compiles it.
The glide_* entries of patch 30's UI table stay as unreferenced defaults.

Drop: never; upstream will not grow a build option for one device.

